# End-of-Turn Change Summary

After making any file changes (edits, creations, deletions), end the response with a concise `SUMMARY` block listing each affected file by its **full workspace-relative path** (with the **filename + extension bolded**) and a **brief parenthetical note** describing the change.

## Format

```
SUMMARY
Modifications:
- <path/to/>**<file.ext>** (<brief change note>)
- <path/to/>**<file.ext>** (<brief change note>)

Created Files:
- <path/to/>**<file.ext>** (<brief purpose>)

Deleted Files:
- <path/to/>**<file.ext>** (<brief reason>)
```

## Rules

- **Always include the `SUMMARY` header** when files were changed.
- **Use workspace-relative paths** (e.g. `frontend/src/lib/components/Button.svelte`), not just basenames.
- **Bold only the filename + extension** using markdown `**...**`. The directory portion stays unbolded. For files at the workspace root, bold the entire name.
- **Add a short parenthetical note** after each entry — a few words on what changed or why. No full sentences, no language tags, no code blocks.
- **Omit empty sections** — if nothing was created, drop `Created Files:` entirely. Same for `Modifications:` and `Deleted Files:`.
- **Skip the summary entirely** when the turn made no file changes (pure Q&A, planning, or read-only exploration).
- **Place the summary last**, after any explanation of the changes.

## Examples

```
✅ GOOD — full paths, filename bolded, brief notes
SUMMARY
Modifications:
- frontend/src/routes/**+page.svelte** (added click handler)
- backend/internal/api/**handlers.go** (new GET /campaigns route)

Created Files:
- frontend/src/lib/components/**CampaignCreateModal.svelte** (new create-campaign modal)
```

```
✅ GOOD — root-level file, entire name bolded
SUMMARY
Modifications:
- **README.md** (added setup section)
```

```
❌ BAD — nothing bolded
SUMMARY
Modifications:
- frontend/src/routes/+page.svelte (added click handler)
```

```
❌ BAD — full path bolded instead of just filename
SUMMARY
Modifications:
- **frontend/src/routes/+page.svelte** (added click handler)
```
